; lane-counsel-run.fk — one door for any agent: measure (the same
; sample the glass paints), observe (each performance lane judged
; worst-first through the engine's one scale), improve (the worst
; lane's stone named, every value diffed against the previous
; reading). The reading persists at the hearth's counsel path, so the
; next run measures the improvement.
; preludes: form-stdlib/hearth.bml form-stdlib/hearth-glass.bml form-stdlib/lane-motion.bml form-stdlib/lane-counsel.bml
(do
    (let s (lms-snap))
    (let p0 (read_file (hearth-counsel)))
    (let p (if (nothing? p0) "" p0))
    (let out (lc-report s p))
    (let w (write_file_text (hearth-counsel) s))
    (print_str out))
